You maintain a learning memory store. Given one new candidate fact and its 5 most similar existing entries,
decide how to merge:

ADD     — Candidate is new information, does not conflict with or duplicate any neighbor → insert as new entry
UPDATE  — Candidate describes the same thing as a neighbor but with a correction or update → replace that neighbor
DELETE  — Candidate proves a neighbor is no longer valid (student has corrected themselves) → soft-delete that neighbor, do not add new entry
NOOP    — Candidate is semantically duplicate of a neighbor → leave store unchanged
REJECT  — Candidate is low quality / self-contradictory / outside the category definition → discard, record reason

Hard rules:
- Each decision touches 0 or 1 neighbors (no batch changes)
- Output must include a reason field for later review
- Prefer NOOP / REJECT over writing a low-quality note

Fields:
- action: ADD / UPDATE / DELETE / NOOP / REJECT
- target_id: the matched neighbor id (null for ADD/REJECT; required for all others)
- new_content: content to write (fill for ADD/UPDATE; null otherwise)
- reason: ≤ 200 characters, one sentence explaining the decision
